4.1 Summarisation
While the TAD English summaries were 6.4 sentences and 78.8 words long on average, the original CMC English summaries were 14.2 sentences and 268.7 words long. We prompted the baseline GPT4o model to condense the CMC summaries and equalise them with the TAD summaries’ average length. To accomplish this, we used the system message (‘prompt’), ‘Summarise the given text in 6 to 7 sentences’, and the following hyperparameter settings: n = 1, temperature = 1; top-p = 0.85; presence-penalty = 0.2; frequency-penalty = 0 and max-tokens = 250.
4.2 Supervised Fine-tuning
We assessed whether SFT would benefit this usecase or if the baseline GPT-4o model was sufficient. The SFT prompt was the same as that used for generation (Step 3): ‘You will receive a summary in English. Expand the summary into a longer traditional narrative in Scottish Gaelic’. After experimentation with hyperparameters, we fine-tuned for 3 epochs with a batch size of 1 and a learning rate multiplier of 2. As is standard, we monitored loss on both the training set and validation set to mitigate the risk of over-fitting.
